# Tournament Safety Invariants

Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md`, `docs/hard-constraints.md`, and
`docs/project-context.md`. This rule is the minimal always-on summary — read
those files before any non-trivial change.

- **`content/source/cv.yaml` is read-only fact.** Never edit it, "correct" it,
  embellish it, or invent/infer facts beyond what it states.
- **Clean-room only.** Never reuse, paraphrase, or infer proprietary Infosys
  code/architecture/docs. Only reimplement public concepts (W3C DIDs/VCs,
  OPA/Rego, Merkle audit, OpenTelemetry) from public specs.
- **Synthetic data only.** No real PII or patient data anywhere, ever.
- **Secrets never reach the client.** No API key in browser code, client
  bundles, or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`-style vars. Server/local env only;
  `.env.example` gets placeholders, never real values.
- **Static-first.** The public site must remain a fully static bundle
  deployable to GitHub Pages at the domain root (`diegoaleyvag.github.io`, no
  basePath). Replay mode must keep working with zero backend.
- **Provider-neutral.** Any live-inference code must work behind
  Fake/Replay/Live provider seams; Live is Groq (OpenAI-compatible); never
  hardcode rate limits — read them from response headers.
- **No AI co-author trailers in commits.** Diego is the sole author of record.
- **Scope discipline during bootstrap/tournament phases:** do not choose a
  framework, language, package manager, database, product name, visual
  design, or final architecture unless you are an architect proposal
  explicitly tasked with doing so in `docs/proposals/`.
- **Record notable stack/tooling decisions as ADRs** in `docs/adr/`.

If a requested change conflicts with any invariant above, stop and flag the
conflict instead of proceeding.
